# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# App.vue resolves its route from window.location.pathname, so a hard load or a
# deep link to /start or /auth/callback must still be served index.html rather
# than 404. The 200 status is a rewrite, not a redirect: the URL stays put and
# the SPA reads it.
#
# NOTE: /api is deliberately NOT rewritten here. The SPA calls the backend at a
# same-origin "/api" (frontend/src/api/client.ts), which means /api must be
# proxied to the Spring Boot origin ahead of this rule -- see
# docs/DOMAIN-AND-EMAIL-SETUP.md. Leaving it out means a misrouted API call fails
# loudly instead of silently returning index.html to a fetch() expecting JSON.
/*    /index.html    200
